WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:03.105
Welcome to episode three.

2
00:00:03.105 --> 00:00:07.981
Today we take our time with knowledge:
everything your assistant knows about your

3
00:00:07.981 --> 00:00:09.847
company, and how it gets there.

4
00:00:09.847 --> 00:00:14.843
You’ll add a real fact yourself, and a few
minutes later the assistant will hand it

5
00:00:14.843 --> 00:00:16.589
back — with the source named.

6
00:00:16.589 --> 00:00:17.913
We’ll go step by step.

7
00:00:17.913 --> 00:00:21.585
This page — knowledge entries —
is where your fact will live.

8
00:00:21.585 --> 00:00:23.030
Let’s look around first.

9
00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:32.993
Let’s start next door, in
Documents — one tab over.

10
00:00:32.993 --> 00:00:37.009
Three files live here
already: the 2026 brand guidelines,

11
00:00:37.009 --> 00:00:39.968
a support review, an onboarding checklist.

12
00:00:39.968 --> 00:00:42.152
And see the tab row at the top?

13
00:00:42.152 --> 00:00:47.859
Documents, knowledge entries, websites,
products — that row is the whole area for

14
00:00:47.859 --> 00:00:48.559
today.

15
00:00:48.559 --> 00:00:52.720
Everything an agent answers from
sits behind one of these tabs.

16
00:00:56.720 --> 00:01:01.313
Now let’s add a fact of our own —
we switch back to Knowledge entries.

17
00:01:01.313 --> 00:01:06.234
Say the team just piloted a new
returns window: sixty days on annual plans.

18
00:01:06.234 --> 00:01:08.202
It’s in nobody’s document yet.

19
00:01:08.202 --> 00:01:13.582
For one sentence of truth, an entry is
the right shape — a document would bury it,

20
00:01:13.582 --> 00:01:16.600
and a record is for
typed values, like prices.

21
00:01:18.820 --> 00:01:20.471
So we click Add entry.

22
00:01:20.471 --> 00:01:23.323
Topic first: the returns policy pilot.

23
00:01:23.323 --> 00:01:27.902
Then the content — one clear
sentence that stands on its own.

24
00:01:27.902 --> 00:01:28.653
And… save.

25
00:01:28.653 --> 00:01:30.529
There it is, in the list.

26
00:01:30.529 --> 00:01:34.357
No deploy, no retraining:
indexing runs on its own,

27
00:01:34.357 --> 00:01:37.660
and we’ll come back to
test this at the end.

28
00:01:46.720 --> 00:01:49.969
Back to Documents, and
this time watch the badges.

29
00:01:49.969 --> 00:01:53.867
Indexed means: the text was
pulled out, split into passages,

30
00:01:53.867 --> 00:01:55.946
and every passage made findable.

31
00:01:55.946 --> 00:01:57.245
Nothing was trained.

32
00:01:57.245 --> 00:02:02.118
Your files change no model and never
leave this workspace — at answer time,

33
00:02:02.118 --> 00:02:04.977
the assistant fetches
the passages it needs,

34
00:02:04.977 --> 00:02:06.017
source attached.

35
00:02:06.017 --> 00:02:09.720
That’s what fed the citations
you checked in episode two.

36
00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.398
One tab over: Products.

37
00:02:14.398 --> 00:02:20.309
Documents hold prose; records hold values
— an agent reads the price from a field

38
00:02:20.309 --> 00:02:23.228
instead of guessing it from a paragraph.

39
00:02:23.228 --> 00:02:25.198
Let’s look one up for real.

40
00:02:25.198 --> 00:02:31.109
We type ‘workshop’ into the search… the
table narrows to one row… and there’s the

41
00:02:31.109 --> 00:02:31.912
price: 950.

42
00:02:31.912 --> 00:02:35.270
An agent doing a quote
reads exactly this row.

43
00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:40.582
Next tab: Websites.

44
00:02:40.582 --> 00:02:46.106
Public sites can join your knowledge too
— let’s walk the dialog without saving.

45
00:02:46.106 --> 00:02:51.492
Add website… a domain… and here’s the
setting that matters: the scan interval.

46
00:02:51.492 --> 00:02:55.704
The crawler re-visits on that
rhythm — hourly at the fastest,

47
00:02:55.704 --> 00:02:57.983
every thirty days at the slowest.

48
00:02:57.983 --> 00:03:01.021
It sees only what an
anonymous visitor sees;

49
00:03:01.021 --> 00:03:04.128
anything behind a login
belongs in Documents.

50
00:03:04.128 --> 00:03:07.030
We’re not really adding this one — Escape.

51
00:03:11.030 --> 00:03:15.248
One question left before the
test: who gets to read all this?

52
00:03:15.248 --> 00:03:20.779
Back in Documents, we open the row menu
on the brand guidelines… and pick Assign

53
00:03:20.779 --> 00:03:21.479
team.

54
00:03:21.479 --> 00:03:26.665
Right now the file is
organization-wide — every member’s agents may use it.

55
00:03:26.665 --> 00:03:30.191
Pick a team instead, and
it stays inside that team.

56
00:03:30.191 --> 00:03:33.648
We leave the guidelines
open to everyone — Cancel.

57
00:03:33.648 --> 00:03:37.174
One note: knowledge
entries don’t have this switch;

58
00:03:37.174 --> 00:03:39.447
they always serve the whole workspace.

59
00:03:43.447 --> 00:03:46.942
On to the chat, for the
failure you’ll actually meet:

60
00:03:46.942 --> 00:03:49.382
not a missing fact — an outdated one.

61
00:03:49.382 --> 00:03:53.866
Last year our accent color was
teal; the 2026 guidelines retired it.

62
00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.515
Would the assistant know?

63
00:03:55.515 --> 00:03:59.801
We ask, exactly like a teammate
would… and watch what comes back.

64
00:04:10.047 --> 00:04:15.492
Read it with me: the teal is retired, the
primary is deep blue — and the source is

65
00:04:15.492 --> 00:04:17.683
named, the brand guidelines file.

66
00:04:17.683 --> 00:04:21.999
The assistant caught this because
someone kept that file current.

67
00:04:21.999 --> 00:04:25.054
If last year’s palette
still sat in Documents,

68
00:04:25.054 --> 00:04:29.105
you’d get the opposite answer,
delivered just as confidently.

69
00:04:29.105 --> 00:04:33.487
So when facts change: stale file
out, one current truth per topic.

70
00:04:36.287 --> 00:04:38.684
And now, the promise from the start.

71
00:04:38.684 --> 00:04:43.678
We open a fresh chat… and ask about
the returns window — the fact we added,

72
00:04:43.678 --> 00:04:44.810
four minutes ago.

73
00:04:44.810 --> 00:04:48.606
No agent was configured,
nothing was deployed in between.

74
00:05:01.287 --> 00:05:06.434
Sixty days on annual plans, thirty
on monthly — and look at the source:

75
00:05:06.434 --> 00:05:11.074
the returns policy pilot, the
exact entry you watched me create.

76
00:05:11.074 --> 00:05:12.959
Fact in, cited answer out.

77
00:05:12.959 --> 00:05:16.728
And every teammate’s chat
gets this same answer now.

78
00:05:20.287 --> 00:05:21.477
That’s the episode.

79
00:05:21.477 --> 00:05:25.609
You added a fact and heard it
cited back, read what Indexed means,

80
00:05:25.609 --> 00:05:29.491
pulled a price from a record,
met the crawler’s scan interval,

81
00:05:29.491 --> 00:05:33.122
and opened the control that
limits a document to one team.

82
00:05:33.122 --> 00:05:37.317
The knowledge section of the docs
goes deeper on every tab you saw.

83
00:05:39.317 --> 00:05:44.208
Next time: agents — you’ll build one
of your own, instructions and all.

84
00:05:44.208 --> 00:05:45.861
See you in episode four.

